---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout current="agent" title="What is an agent?">
  <section class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Definition</p>
      <h1>Agents are models in a control loop.</h1>
      <p>
        Prompting asks once. An agent keeps state, chooses tools, observes what
        happened, and decides whether to continue.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="agent-grid">
      <aside class="definition-card">
        <span>LLM agent</span>
        <p>
          A goal-directed program where an LLM repeatedly decides the next
          action, uses tools, reads observations, and updates state until the
          task is done.
        </p>
        <small>Framing synthesized from Google Cloud and Hugging Face agent docs.</small>
      </aside>

      <div class="loop-card" aria-label="Agent execution loop">
        <div class="loop-node">
          <span>01</span>
          <strong>User goal</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="loop-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="loop-node">
          <span>02</span>
          <strong>Decide</strong>
          <em>LLM selects action</em>
        </div>
        <div class="loop-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="loop-node">
          <span>03</span>
          <strong>Act</strong>
          <em>tool / code / search / API</em>
        </div>
        <div class="loop-arrow down" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div class="loop-node observe">
          <span>04</span>
          <strong>Observe</strong>
          <em>result returns</em>
        </div>
        <div class="loop-arrow back" aria-hidden="true">←</div>
        <div class="loop-node repeat">
          <span>05</span>
          <strong>Update or stop</strong>
          <em>plan, state, done</em>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="code-card">
      <figcaption>
        <span>agent_loop.py</span>
        <span>pseudocode</span>
      </figcaption>
      <pre><code>while not done:
    context = build_context(state, memory, user_goal)
    action = llm.decide(context, available_tools)
    observation = execute(action)
    state = update_state(state, action, observation)
    done = should_stop(state, observation)</code></pre>
    </figure>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
